WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:12.120
We’ve had our first regular council meeting
of the year for the February meeting.

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:17.380
It wasn’t a particularly demanding meeting,
but we did start the meeting with a moment’s

00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:22.190
silence in memory of Karen Eastwood, who recently
died.

00:00:22.190 --> 00:00:26.870
She’s a member of the Wooden-Sefton Community
board.

00:00:26.870 --> 00:00:32.930
Also for Peter McMorran from Oxford who was
a past councillor and the last chair of Oxford

00:00:32.930 --> 00:00:34.750
County Council.

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:38.961
And Richard Cocker who was one of our staff
members who worked for quite a long time with

00:00:38.961 --> 00:00:40.620
the building unit.

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:46.190
We also acknowledged the three local recipients
of honours in the New Year’s Honours list,

00:00:46.190 --> 00:00:49.030
so that was a nicer thing to be able to do.

00:00:49.030 --> 00:00:52.600
The meeting itself, I guess there were two
main areas of discussion.

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:58.679
One was our submission to a parliamentary
select committee on a government proposal

00:00:58.679 --> 00:01:05.890
to shift the responsibility for fluoridating
water from councils to district health boards.

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:10.460
None of the water supply in Waimakariri is
fluoridated, and in my time I’ve had very

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:12.520
little demand for that to happen.

00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:17.530
Our preference is that it’s a national issue
related to dental health and it should be

00:01:17.530 --> 00:01:20.890
dealt with nationally.

00:01:20.890 --> 00:01:26.710
The other matter that we dealt with at the
council meeting. We looked at the question

00:01:26.710 --> 00:01:30.910
whether we should have an independent member
of our audit and risk committee.

00:01:30.910 --> 00:01:37.560
A number of councils around the country do
that, but in the end our council decided that

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:42.390
with the quality of our staff and the kind of oversight
that we can give as elected members – we

00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:43.890
didn’t need to do that.

